WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.484
A screening test only helps if someone acts on the result.

00:00:04.567 --> 00:00:09.818
In a study of more than thirty-two thousand adults with a positive stool test, only

00:00:09.957 --> 00:00:14.652
fifty-six percent completed a follow-up colonoscopy within a year.

00:00:14.819 --> 00:00:19.570
Every transfer creates a chance for responsibility to become unclear.

00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:23.487
Suhail Health gives each result a visible route to care.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.364
Meet Mariam, a fictional patient in this demo.

00:00:27.781 --> 00:00:32.698
Her result arrives in a worklist with an owner, a next action, and a deadline.

00:00:33.198 --> 00:00:37.866
Navigators can find overdue work, rejected transfers, and cases that need

00:00:37.949 --> 00:00:43.367
assignment. Open a completed case to see dates, service targets, and the evidence

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.951
behind each step, from the result through closure.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:51.304
On her phone, Mariam can see where she is in the journey.

00:00:51.721 --> 00:00:53.971
Her result message arrives in Arabic.

00:00:54.304 --> 00:00:56.972
It explains what happens next and who will help.

00:00:57.472 --> 00:01:01.556
She can confirm receipt and answer two questions to check understanding.

00:01:01.972 --> 00:01:05.306
If she needs help, her navigator gets a task to call her.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.057
Her care team is easy to reach.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.591
Clinicians bring assigned episodes and patient questions into one workspace.

00:01:14.008 --> 00:01:17.633
Human replies record an agreed action and owner.

00:01:17.925 --> 00:01:20.925
Specialists see their assigned consultations.

00:01:21.175 --> 00:01:25.343
Optional AI assistance prepares source-linked drafts for review.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.343
The care team makes the clinical decisions.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.287
Receiving services see a minimum referral packet.

00:01:32.704 --> 00:01:36.871
They explicitly accept a referral or record a rejection reason.

00:01:37.371 --> 00:01:41.789
Appointment controls keep booking, attendance, and no-shows distinct.

00:01:42.206 --> 00:01:47.123
A proposed transfer keeps the sending owner accountable until the receiver accepts

00:01:47.165 --> 00:01:49.040
the intended responsibility.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.467
An urgent result goes straight to a clinician on a sixty-minute clock, with an

00:01:54.551 --> 00:01:57.385
on-call backup and no model in that path.

00:01:57.885 --> 00:02:02.510
To close required care, an authorized clinician needs verified evidence of the

00:02:02.552 --> 00:02:06.678
investigation, the reviewed outcome, and the patient update.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:09.803
The checklist shows exactly what is missing.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:15.978
Operations can see time to notification, understanding, and completed care,

00:02:16.061 --> 00:02:21.729
and where work is stalled. In a simulated cohort calibrated to published studies,

00:02:21.812 --> 00:02:27.313
estimated follow-up completion rises from fifty-six to sixty-nine percent within a

00:02:27.396 --> 00:02:31.147
year. A pilot would measure the effect in practice.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:35.629
Six bounded agents prepare drafts and check records.

00:02:35.837 --> 00:02:38.754
The care team remains responsible for decisions.

00:02:39.005 --> 00:02:43.922
Fifteen hundred automated safety checks passed, including five hundred correctly

00:02:44.005 --> 00:02:49.340
refused premature closures. We are seeking a partner for a twelve-week pilot on one

00:02:49.423 --> 00:02:52.215
screening pathway. Suhail Health.

00:02:52.423 --> 00:02:54.757
Guiding every result to care.
